    "pages": [21],
    "source_label": "Example 1.22",
    "question": {
      "text": "Find the real numbers x and y such that (x + iy)(3 − 2i) = 6 − 17i.",
      "tex": "(x + iy)(3 - 2i) = 6 - 17i"
    },
    "steps": [
      {
        "text": "Expand the product on the left using the multiplication rule and i² = −1.",
        "tex": "(x + iy)(3 - 2i) = 3x - 2xi + 3yi - 2y\\,i^2 = (3x + 2y) + (3y - 2x)\\,i"
      },
      {
        "text": "Two complex numbers are equal when their real parts are equal and their imaginary parts are equal.",
        "tex": "3x + 2y = 6, \\qquad 3y - 2x = -17"
      },
      {
        "text": "Solve the pair of equations: from the first, 2y = 6 − 3x; substituting into the second gives 3y − 2x = −17, so multiply the first by 2 and the second by 3 to eliminate y.",
        "tex": "6x + 4y = 12, \\quad -6x + 9y = -51 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; 13y = -39 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; y = -3"
      },
      {
        "text": "Substitute back to find x.",
        "tex": "3x + 2(-3) = 6 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; 3x = 12 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; x = 4"
      }
    ],
    "answer_tex": "x = 4, \\quad y = -3",
    "review": { "status": "developer-test", "reviewed_by": null, "date": null }
  }
]
